	(36, NULL, 509, 'Conference', 'Grid Simulation and Real Time Agent visualization ', 'R.Chitra', 'Grid-based simulations are widely used in fields such as robotics, artificial intelligence, game development, and traffic management to study the movement and interaction of multiple agents in a structured environment. This project focuses on the design and implementation of a Grid Simulation and Real-Time Agent Visualization system that enables agents to navigate within a two-dimensional grid while adhering to boundary constraints and avoiding collisions with other agents. The simulation operates using discrete time steps, allowing the positions of agents to be updated dynamically as they move through the grid environment. ', 'MATLAB , Python , Sensors', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Published', NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, '2026-03-21', 'Tirunelveli Dhakshina Mara Nadar Sangam College in Assocation withXavier Institute for Research and Development', NULL, '/uploads/faculty/chitra_r/research/research_chitra_r_1774536479993_8161451.pdf', 'International', '2026-03-26 14:47:59', '2026-03-26 14:47:59'),
